	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Type `pw` followed by a domain (github.com) to list its accounts: ↵ copies the password, ⌘↵ the username, ⌥↵ the one-time code. Type `pwg` to generate a strong password, or `pwg &lt;domain&gt; &lt;username&gt;` to also save it; `pwg` also lists the last 20 generated passwords. Options change one generation: a length (4-40), `apple`, `+l`/`-l` letters, `+d`/`-d` digits, `+s`/`-s` symbols, `+a`/`-a` look-alikes (`pwg 24 -s`). Defaults are in Configure Workflow.

Passwords are copied straight to the clipboard, marked concealed so clipboard histories skip them; they never go through Alfred. Generated passwords are kept in an encrypted file whose key is in your login Keychain.

Requires apw (https://github.com/bendews/apw): `brew install bendews/homebrew-tap/apw`, `brew services start apw`, then `pw pin` to pair it after each restart.</string>
